# rundeck — real-world examples

Rundeck is a job-scheduler / runbook-automation server. Requires Java 1.7+.

## Installation (RPM-based)

```sh
rpm -Uvh http://repo.rundeck.org/latest.rpm
yum install rundeck
service rundeckd start
```

## Installation notes for the homelab (Tumbleweed)

```sh
# No native zypper package; run the official container instead
sudo zypper install docker
sudo systemctl enable --now docker

docker run -d --name rundeck \
  -p 4440:4440 \
  -e RUNDECK_GRAILS_URL=http://homelab:4440 \
  rundeck/rundeck:5.0.0

# Then browse to http://homelab:4440 (default login admin/admin — change it)
```

## Rundeck CLI (rd)

```sh
# Legacy dispatch command: run `id` on all nodes tagged www in project "anvils"
dispatch -p anvils --follow -I tags=www -- id

# Modern `rd` CLI equivalents:
rd projects list
rd jobs list -p anvils
rd run -p anvils -j "backups/nightly-media"     # run a job by group/name
rd adhoc -p anvils -f --filter 'tags: www' -- uptime
```

## Flag / arg reference (dispatch & rd)

| Item | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-p <project>` | Target project |
| `--follow` / `-f` | Stream output as it runs |
| `-I tags=<t>` | Include nodes matching a tag |
| `--filter '<q>'` | Node filter query (rd) |
| `-- <cmd>` | Command to run on matched nodes |
| `-j <group/name>` | Job identifier for `rd run` |
